From dd79f0e80bc42aec1a5cfe66420018aaedf4570e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 15:27:15 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] dos: patch 0196 -- releasing a nested hold keeps a paused
 MIDI replay held

SDL_DOSMidiDeferHold(false) cleared g_mdq_hold unconditionally. The
Opl3Detect/InitChip/Shutdown wrappers hold around their own chip writes
and release after, so if one ran while SDL_DOSMidiDeferPause(true) held
the replay -- a second OPL sink opened during a music pause -- the release
lifted the pause's hold and the SB ISR played the paused song's queued
writes (up to the ~2 s planned ahead) while the port believed it was
paused, then resume shifted stamps that had already played. Releasing to
g_mdq_paused keeps the pause's hold; SDL_DOSMidiDeferPause(false) and
SDL_DOSMidiDeferEnable(0) remain the only ways out of a pause.

Found by the /sdldos:review of 0195 (dosags PLAN.md, 2026-09-23); no
fixture hit it.
---
 src/audio/dos/SDL_dosaudio_sb.c | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/audio/dos/SDL_dosaudio_sb.c b/src/audio/dos/SDL_dosaudio_sb.c
index 780b901ee..f2355e51d 100644
--- a/src/audio/dos/SDL_dosaudio_sb.c
+++ b/src/audio/dos/SDL_dosaudio_sb.c
@@ -1861,7 +1861,11 @@ bool SDL_DOSMidiDeferHold(bool hold)
         g_mdq_hold = 1;
         return true;
     }
-    g_mdq_hold = 0;
+    /* DOS-PORT patch 0196: a paused replay stays held. The Detect/InitChip/
+       Shutdown wrappers hold around their own chip writes and release after;
+       releasing to 0 lifted SDL_DOSMidiDeferPause's hold too, and the ISR
+       played the paused song's queued writes (~2 s) while the port was paused. */
+    g_mdq_hold = g_mdq_paused ? 1 : 0;
     return true;
 }
 
